{"lines":[{"w":0.20300148010253904,"x":0.0827298713474931,"t":"Sample Writing answers","y":0.05718325712890493,"c":1,"h":0.021363648774325172},{"t":"TEST 4, WRITING TASK 1","x":0.081314880963670413,"y":0.10741777489452264,"w":0.30449826558430992,"h":0.020643806857942648,"c":1},{"y":0.14520643780186604,"t":"This is an answer written by a candidate who achieved a Band 6 score.","h":0.017584260149048792,"x":0.081314885045238872,"w":0.58650517781575529,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.66782007853190106,"x":0.08131487414210023,"t":"In this chart, we can see a representation of categories and satisfaction of library","y":0.17284814569303186,"h":0.020465808118282247},{"w":0.6783009338378907,"c":1,"x":0.082998564336634592,"y":0.19465364090904103,"t":"users, the first feature that we pay attention is the users majority take part of full-","h":0.019731471553559587},{"w":0.71453287760416673,"h":0.018909588487436846,"t":"time undergraduate and full-time post-graduate, such as they probably are the biggest","y":0.21656976747020174,"x":0.083044979799745608,"c":1},{"w":0.69723185221354167,"t":"data of library satisfaction, since very satistied until not satistied, also post-graduate","x":0.083044973455922669,"h":0.017535437229548867,"c":1,"y":0.23827851653589316},{"y":0.25857242833102378,"x":0.083044977246791329,"t":"students would need more special materials to hardest researchs and learning method,","h":0.020643806857942648,"w":0.72145329793294266,"c":1},{"y":0.28052325584259608,"x":0.083044987451228666,"t":"Even thought undergraduates students, fresh or veteran, are o their initial academic","w":0.69377161661783848,"h":0.018986890831554248,"c":1},{"w":0.71626296997070316,"y":0.30087209305170082,"h":0.018931965464224265,"c":1,"x":0.083044985521131598,"t":"career, both categaries look satisfied with the library between another may, as the fact"},{"x":0.083044980275460797,"w":0.33391003926595048,"h":0.017513060252761559,"c":1,"y":0.32260321909127088,"t":"they use it more than once during a day."},{"x":0.083044972855781135,"h":0.018995028096032818,"w":0.68166091918945304,"t":"On the other hand, academic staff is the lowest data categorie that use the library,","y":0.35164450675354997,"c":1},{"y":0.37193841859505472,"w":0.67474049886067722,"t":"with a percentage of 17%, the reason beyond this effect is because the staffs must","h":0.019049953463362801,"c":1,"x":0.083044975417216491},{"h":0.01898078838372419,"y":0.39389534886547106,"c":1,"x":0.083044981110136334,"t":"to focus on their work, so they probally use the library on their free-time, however,","w":0.67647059122721342},{"x":0.083044977302818096,"y":0.41424418571576394,"t":"distance learning students have a 8% percentage, both categaries have a 1% difference","w":0.72145329793294266,"h":0.020348837861153823,"c":1},{"w":0.6696667989095052,"h":0.020549903640052936,"c":1,"t":"percentage, which explain they took a little part of satisfaction research, distance","x":0.082981433763319498,"y":0.43467356349482889},{"c":1,"y":0.45784883692766631,"x":0.083044981114920133,"w":0.67647059122721354,"t":"learning have a low percentage because the fact they also access online materials.","h":0.01744186102384615},{"c":1,"t":"Finally, part-time postgraduate students are the medium date, with a 16% percentage.","h":0.021885955308683203,"x":0.08300006772559726,"y":0.48517618077008429,"w":0.72153147379557292},{"y":0.50726744156962522,"x":0.083044984044397169,"h":0.017575105809931824,"c":1,"t":"where they would use the libraray to classroom researchs or homeworks.","w":0.60034601847330726},{"h":0.01308139510051276,"y":0.54360465127845847,"w":0.26989618937174481,"x":0.086505192390027519,"c":1,"t":"Here is the examiner's comment:"},{"y":0.56682995126056335,"t":"This is generally a good response, there is an introduction at the start, and an","w":0.64186848958333342,"c":1,"h":0.017494751574527734,"x":0.12283738141599447},{"c":1,"w":0.67128026326497403,"x":0.12283737714867253,"t":"attempt at an overview [....the users majority take part of full-time undergraduate","y":0.58430232529313153,"h":0.017517128551314931},{"y":0.60319767444694583,"x":0.12283737692856098,"w":0.67128026326497392,"h":0.01891569160263884,"c":1,"t":"and full-time post-graduate, such as they probably are the biggest data of library"},{"y":0.62023641278223707,"c":1,"t":"satisfaction]. To improve the overview, there should be a summary across both","x":0.12278759497683618,"w":0.64888615926106763,"h":0.020278998735987042},{"w":0.65397923787434897,"c":1,"t":"charts. Key data from the pie chart is presented quite well but the 'Library user","y":0.63953488343862896,"x":0.12283737059365857,"h":0.017567985620091542},{"h":0.020281758985792986,"t":"satisfaction' data is not sufficiently covered. There are also examples of irrelevant","x":0.12105896940889144,"w":0.67483383178710943,"c":1,"y":0.65669471887405617},{"t":"information [would need more special materials | use it more than once during a","x":0.12100349627585218,"y":0.67205572825057358,"h":0.022878786998665968,"w":0.66977656046549483,"c":1},{"h":0.01744186102384615,"c":1,"w":0.67128026326497392,"t":"day use the library on their free-time] which can detract from task achievement.","x":0.12283737691887381,"y":0.6947674415784969},{"h":0.017588328447602164,"w":0.62975779215494787,"t":"Ideas are mostly arranged logically. There are some nice linking expressions","x":0.1211072630027805,"c":1,"y":0.7207837648524611},{"t":"[since | also | so | Finally | On the other hand] with some slips [Even thought \/","x":0.1211072750629099,"h":0.018988925648202759,"c":1,"y":0.73827851617862617,"w":0.64878890991210947},{"c":1,"t":"Even though], and some good examples of reference [their | they].","h":0.017536454304187266,"y":0.75717284829186027,"w":0.5536332194010416,"x":0.12283736961414624},{"y":0.78341497579461383,"w":0.59515569051106776,"c":1,"t":"Vocabulary is mainly appropriate and spelling is generally well managed","h":0.018910605562075244,"x":0.12283737972353753},{"w":0.56574396769205726,"x":0.12110725483655226,"y":0.80230930725093774,"t":"[representation | pay attention]; some errors remain but don't affect","h":0.017494751574527623,"c":1},{"x":0.12283737252979914,"h":0.018912640378723755,"w":0.63148788452148441,"c":1,"y":0.82120363865712276,"t":"understanding. Grammatical structures are mixed, but there are multi clause"},{"y":0.83866279072127581,"c":1,"t":"sentences and examples of a range of structures, including modal verbs used","h":0.018929931314947579,"x":0.12283737570705265,"w":0.64013839721679688},{"y":0.85755813925095281,"h":0.017529334781718808,"w":0.50519032796223962,"c":1,"t":"correctly [would need], and with some errors [must to focus].","x":0.12283736190431294},{"x":0.083044983253625401,"h":0.013081395100512871,"c":1,"y":0.95784883727400372,"w":0.032871971130371089,"t":"136"}],"w":2400,"h":2857}